#000000;\n   271→            }\n   272→\n   273→            a:after {\n   274→                content: \" (\" attr(href) \")\";\n   275→                font-size: 8pt;\n   276→                color: #828282;\n   277→            }\n   278→        }\n   279→\n   280→        .highlight {\n   281→            background-color: #ffffcc;\n   282→            padding: 2px 4px;\n   283→        }\n   284→\n   285→        .insight-link {\n   286→            color: #000000;\n   287→            font-weight: bold;\n   288→        }\n   289→\n   290→        .insight-link:hover {\n   291→            color: #ff6600;\n   292→        }\n   293→    </style>\n   294→</head>\n   295→<body>\n   296→    <header>\n   297→        <div class=\"container\">\n   298→            <div class=\"header-content\">\n   299→                <div class=\"logo\">\n   300→                    <a href=\"#\">Agentic Coding Research Report</a>\n   301→                </div>\n   302→                <div class=\"date\">\n   303→                    2026-06-11\n   304→                </div>\n   305→                <nav class=\"nav-links\">\n   306→                    <a href=\"#new-products\">New Products</a>\n   307→                    <a href=\"#whitelist-updates\">Updates</a>\n   308→                    <a href=\"#technical-insights\">Insights</a>\n   309→                </nav>\n   310→            </div>\n   311→        </div>\n   312→    </header>\n   313→\n   314→    <main class=\"container\">\n   315→        <div class=\"three-column-layout\">\n   316→            <!-- New Products Section -->\n   317→            <section class=\"new-products section\" id=\"new-products\">\n   318→                <h2 class=\"section-title\">New Products</h2>\n   319→\n   320→                <div class=\"item\">\n   321→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   322→                        <a href=\"https://github.blog/news-insights/product-news/github-copilot-meet-the-new-coding-agent/\">GitHub Copilot Coding Agent</a>\n   323→                    </div>\n   324→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   325→                        GitHub's new Copilot coding agent launched in June 2025, designed to handle complex coding tasks with autonomous agent capabilities.\n   326→                    </div>\n   327→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   328→                        <span class=\"tag\">AI coding agent</span>\n   329→                        <span class=\"source\">GitHub Blog</span>\n   330→                        <span class=\"date\">2025-06-04</span>\n   331→                    </div>\n   332→                </div>\n   333→\n   334→                <div class=\"item\">\n   335→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   336→                        <a href=\"https://factory.ai/news/factory-is-ga\">Factory AI Droids</a>\n   337→                    </div>\n   338→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   339→                        World's first comprehensive AI agents covering the entire software development lifecycle (SDLC), not just coding. Generally Available (GA) as of May 28, 2025.\n   340→                    </div>\n   341→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   342→                        <span class=\"tag\">AI SDLC agent</span>\n   343→                        <span class=\"source\">Factory.ai</span>\n   344→                        <span class=\"date\">2025-05-28</span>\n   345→                    </div>\n   346→                </div>\n   347→\n   348→                <div class=\"item\">\n   349→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   350→                        <a href=\"https://www.prnewswire.com/il/news-releases/bit-cloud-launches-hope-ai-enabling-developers-to-build-complex-applications-in-a-few-hours-302466854.html\">Hope AI</a>\n   351→                    </div>\n   352→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   353→                        Enables developers to build complex applications in just a few hours by bridging the gap between simple low-code tools and professional-grade software development.\n   354→                    </div>\n   355→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   356→                        <span class=\"tag\">AI dev platform</span>\n   357→                        <span class=\"source\">PR Newswire</span>\n   358→                        <span class=\"date\">2025-05-28</span>\n   359→                    </div>\n   360→                </div>\n   361→            </section>\n   362→\n   363→            <!-- Whitelist Updates Section -->\n   364→            <section class=\"whitelist-updates section\" id=\"whitelist-updates\">\n   365→                <h2 class=\"section-title\">Whitelist Updates</h2>\n   366→\n   367→                <div class=\"item\">\n   368→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   369→                        <a href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2026/05/30/github-copilots-new-token-based-billing-spurs-consternation-among-devs/\">GitHub Copilot: Token-Based Billing Model Transition</a>\n   370→                    </div>\n   371→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   372→                        GitHub transitioned all Copilot subscribers from request-based billing (PRUs) to usage-based token-based billing starting June 1, 2026.\n   373→                    </div>\n   374→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   375→                        <span class=\"update-badge update-announcement\">Announcement</span>\n   376→                        <span class=\"date\">2026-06-01</span>\n   377→                    </div>\n   378→                    <div class=\"community-quote sentiment-negative\">\n   379→                        \"GitHub Copilot's new credit-based pricing is highway robbery. My projected bill next month... $847 per month\"\n   380→                        <div class=\"quote-source\">— Reddit (negative sentiment)</div>\n   381→                    </div>\n   382→                </div>\n   383→\n   384→                <div class=\"item\">\n   385→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   386→                        <a href=\"https://docs.github.com/en/copilot/visual-studio\">GitHub Copilot: Visual Studio May 2026 Update</a>\n   387→                    </div>\n   388→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   389→                        GitHub announced the May 2026 update for GitHub Copilot in Visual Studio 2026, introducing a new Plan agent for better project planning.\n   390→                    </div>\n   391→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   392→                        <span class=\"update-badge update-feature\">Feature</span>\n   393→                        <span class=\"date\">2026-06-04</span>\n   394→                    </div>\n   395→                </div>\n   396→\n   397→                <div class=\"item\">\n   398→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   399→                        <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=48196867\">Gemini CLI: Shutdown and Antigravity CLI Replacement</a>\n   400→                    </div>\n   401→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   402→                        Google announced the complete shutdown of Gemini CLI scheduled for June 18, 2026, with all requests returning HTTP 410 errors.\n   403→                    </div>\n   404→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   405→                        <span class=\"update-badge update-announcement\">Announcement</span>\n   406→                        <span class=\"date\">2026-06-18</span>\n   407→                    </div>\n   408→                    <div class=\"community-quote sentiment-negative\">\n   409→                        \"The transition affects all CLI workflows and could break CI/CD pipelines if not addressed\"\n   410→                        <div class=\"quote-source\">— Community discussions (negative sentiment)</div>\n   411→                    </div>\n   412→                </div>\n   413→\n   414→                <div class=\"item\">\n   415→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   416→                        <a href=\"https://changelog.continue.dev/\">Continue: Enhanced MCP Support and Streamlined Editing</a>\n   417→                    </div>\n   418→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   419→                        Continue.dev released a significant update on June 13, 2026, featuring enhanced Model Context Protocol (MCP) support and streamlined editing workflow.\n   420→                    </div>\n   421→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   422→                        <span class=\"update-badge update-feature\">Feature</span>\n   423→                        <span class=\"date\">2026-06-13</span>\n   424→                    </div>\n   425→                </div>\n   426→\n   427→                <div class=\"item\">\n   428→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   429→                        <a href=\"https://docs.devin.ai/release-notes/2026\">Devin: 2026 Release with Enterprise Features</a>\n   430→                    </div>\n   431→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   432→                        Devin released updates in 2026 including enterprise features and developer productivity improvements.\n   433→                    </div>\n   434→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   435→                        <span class=\"update-badge update-feature\">Feature</span>\n   436→                        <span class=\"date\">2026-05-26</span>\n   437→                    </div>\n   438→                    <div class=\"community-quote sentiment-positive\">\n   439→                        \"Cognition's Scott Wu says AI coding agents shouldn't replace humans\"\n   440→                        <div class=\"quote-source\">— TechCrunch (positive sentiment)</div>\n   441→                    </div>\n   442→                </div>\n   443→\n   444→                <div class=\"item\">\n   445→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   446→                        <a href=\"https://cursor.com/changelog\">Cursor: June 2026 Component Styling and Chart Customization</a>\n   447→                    </div>\n   448→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   449→                        Cursor released updates on June 3, 2026, including improved component styling and added chart customization functionality.\n   450→                    </div>\n   451→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   452→                        <span class=\"update-badge update-feature\">Feature</span>\n   453→                        <span class=\"date\">2026-06-03</span>\n   454→                    </div>\n   455→                </div>\n   456→\n   457→                <div class=\"item\">\n   458→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   459→                        <a href=\"https://aider.chat/HISTORY.html\">Aider: v0.77.0 Language Support Expansion</a>\n   460→                    </div>\n   461→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   462→                        Aider released version v0.77.0 with a major upgrade adding 130 new programming languages with linter support via tree-sitter-language-pack.\n   463→                    </div>\n   464→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   465→                        <span class=\"update-badge update-release\">Release</span>\n   466→                        <span class=\"date\">2026-03-01</span>\n   467→                    </div>\n   468→                </div>\n   469→\n   470→                <div class=\"item\">\n   471→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   472→                        <a href=\"https://levelup.gitconnected.com/stop-hitting-the-5-hour-wall-anthropic-just-doubled-my-claude-code-limits-after-6-months-of-0fd5c2ddca46\">Claude Code: Rate Limit Changes and Model Updates</a>\n   473→                    </div>\n   474→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   475→                        Anthropic announced changes to Claude Code rate limits in May 2026, following 6 months of restrictions.\n   476→                    </div>\n   477→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   478→                        <span class=\"update-badge update-announcement\">Announcement</span>\n   479→                        <span class=\"date\">2026-05-06</span>\n   480→                    </div>\n   481→                </div>\n   482→\n   483→                <div class=\"item\">\n   484→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   485→                        <a href=\"https://windsurf.com/blog/changelist-feb25\">Windsurf: Wave 3 Updates and Enhanced Features</a>\n   486→                    </div>\n   487→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   488→                        Windsurf released Wave 3 updates including better credit tracking, revamped Turbo Mode, and customizable app icons for Mac users.\n   489→                    </div>\n   490→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   491→                        <span class=\"update-badge update-feature\">Feature</span>\n   492→                        <span class=\"date\">2026-02-01</span>\n   493→                    </div>\n   494→                </div>\n   495→            </section>\n   496→\n   497→            <!-- Technical Insights Section -->\n   498→            <section class=\"technical-insights section\" id=\"technical-insights\">\n   499→                <h2 class=\"section-title\">Technical Insights</h2>\n   500→\n   501→                <div class=\"item\">\n   502→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   503→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jun/5/openai-help-lockdown-mode/\" class=\"insight-link\">OpenAI Launches Lockdown Mode to Prevent Data Exfiltration</a>\n   504→                    </div>\n   505→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   506→                        OpenAI released Lockdown Mode to help prevent the final stage of data exfiltration from prompt injection attacks by limiting outbound network requests.\n   507→                    </div>\n   508→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   509→                        <span class=\"source\">Simon Willison</span>\n   510→                        <span class=\"date\">2026-06-05</span>\n   511→                    </div>\n   512→                    <div style=\"margin-top: 8px;\">\n   513→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">security</span>\n   514→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">prompt-injection</span>\n   515→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">data-exfiltration</span>\n   516→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">llms</span>\n   517→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">openai</span>\n   518→                    </div>\n   519→                </div>\n   520→\n   521→                <div class=\"item\">\n   522→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   523→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jun/4/ai-enthusiists-skeptics/\" class=\"insight-link\">AI Enthusiasts vs. Skeptics: Race Against Time vs. Entropy</a>\n   524→                    </div>\n   525→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   526→                        Charity Majors captures the dynamic between AI enthusiasts and skeptics: enthusiasts race against time while skeptics race against entropy.\n   527→                    </div>\n   528→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   529→                        <span class=\"source\">Simon Willison</span>\n   530→                        <span class=\"date\">2026-06-04</span>\n   531→                    </div>\n   532→                    <div style=\"margin-top: 8px;\">\n   533→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">ai</span>\n   534→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">engineering-culture</span>\n   535→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">organizational-design</span>\n   536→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">agentic-engineering</span>\n   537→                    </div>\n   538→                </div>\n   539→            </section>\n   540→        </div>\n   541→    </main>\n   542→\n   543→    <footer>\n   544→        <div class=\"container\">\n   545→            <p>\n   546→                <a href=\"#\">Agentic Coding Research Report</a> |\n   547→                <a href=\"#new-products\">New Products</a> |\n   548→                <a href=\"#whitelist-updates\">Updates</a> |\n   549→                <a href=\"#technical-insights\">Insights</a>\n   550→            </p>\n   551→            <p style=\"margin-top: 10px; font-size: 8pt;\">\n   552→                Generated on 2026-06-11 • Updated daily with the latest in agentic coding tools and insights\n   553→            </p>\n   554→        </div>\n   555→    </footer>\n   556→</body>\n   557→</html>\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"
      }
