  <section class=\"whitelist-updates\" id=\"whitelist-updates\">\n   374→                <h2 class=\"section-header\">Product Updates</h2>\n   375→\n   376→                <div class=\"item\">\n   377→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   378→                        <a href=\"https://dev.to/alexmercedcoder/ai-weekly-claude-code-dominates-mcp-goes-mainstream-week-of-march-5-2026-15af\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\n   379→                            Claude Code: Claude Opus 4.8 and Enhanced Features\n   380→                        </a>\n   381→                    </div>\n   382→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   383→                        Anthropic released Claude Opus 4.8 with improvements across coding and agentic tasks. The platform also doubled Claude Code rate limits for developers and introduced enhanced agent usage plans with nested sub-agents, smarter model handling, and new plugin search functionality.\n   384→                    </div>\n   385→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   386→                        <span class=\"badge badge-feature\">FEATURE</span>\n   387→                        <span>📅 2026-05-28</span>\n   388→                        <span class=\"source\">Via: dev.to</span>\n   389→                    </div>\n   390→                </div>\n   391→\n   392→                <div class=\"item\">\n   393→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   394→                        <a href=\"https://cursor.com/changelog\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\n   395→                            Cursor: Design Mode, Organizations, and Auto-Review\n   396→                        </a>\n   397→                    </div>\n   398→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   399→                        Cursor released major updates including Design Mode for browser and canvas editing, multi-select elements, voice input, custom stores and tools in SDK, auto-review run mode, and Organizations for Enterprise customers with improved team management.\n   400→                    </div>\n   401→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   402→                        <span class=\"badge badge-feature\">FEATURE</span>\n   403→                        <span>📅 2026-06-05</span>\n   404→                        <span class=\"source\">Via: cursor.com</span>\n   405→                    </div>\n   406→                </div>\n   407→\n   408→                <div class=\"item\">\n   409→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   410→                        <a href=\"https://github.com/features/copilot/whats-new\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\n   411→                            GitHub Copilot: Microsoft Build 2026 Agent Features and Policy Changes\n   412→                        </a>\n   413→                    </div>\n   414→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   415→                        GitHub announced major Copilot updates at Microsoft Build 2026 including agent-native desktop experience, CLI improvements with voice input and rubber duck feature, and new proprietary AI models. On June 1, 2026, GitHub began using Copilot interactions to train their AI models.\n   416→                    </div>\n   417→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   418→                        <span class=\"badge badge-announcement\">ANNOUNCEMENT</span>\n   419→                        <span>📅 2026-06-02</span>\n   420→                        <span class=\"source\">Via: github.com</span>\n   421→                    </div>\n   422→                </div>\n   423→\n   424→                <div class=\"item\">\n   425→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   426→                        <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/changelog/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\n   427→                            Codex CLI: GPT-5.3-Codex-Spark and GPT-5.3-Codex Launch\n   428→                        </a>\n   429→                    </div>\n   430→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   431→                        OpenAI released GPT-5.3-Codex-Spark, a research preview model optimized for real-time coding delivering over 1000 tokens per second, and GPT-5.3-Codex, the most capable agentic coding model. Both models feature stronger reasoning, better collaboration, and 25% faster performance.\n   432→                    </div>\n   433→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   434→                        <span class=\"badge badge-feature\">FEATURE</span>\n   435→                        <span>📅 2026-02-12</span>\n   436→                        <span class=\"source\">Via: developers.openai.com</span>\n   437→                    </div>\n   438→                </div>\n   439→\n   440→                <div class=\"item\">\n   441→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   442→                        <a href=\"https://geminicli.com/docs/changelogs/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\n   443→                            Gemini CLI: v0.43.0 with Surgical Code Edits and Session Portability\n   444→                        </a>\n   445→                    </div>\n   446→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   447→                        Google released Gemini CLI v0.43.0 featuring surgical code edits using the edit tool, session export and import functionality for portability, and adaptive token estimation for better context management efficiency.\n   448→                    </div>\n   449→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   450→                        <span class=\"badge badge-release\">RELEASE</span>\n   451→                        <span>📅 2026-05-22</span>\n   452→                        <span class=\"source\">Via: geminicli.com</span>\n   453→                    </div>\n   454→                </div>\n   455→            </section>\n   456→\n   457→            <!-- Technical Insights Section -->\n   458→            <section class=\"technical-insights\" id=\"technical-insights\">\n   459→                <h2 class=\"section-header\">Technical Insights</h2>\n   460→\n   461→                <div class=\"item\">\n   462→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   463→                        <a href=\"https://www.marktechpost.com/2026/06/10/ai-coding-agents-development-platforms-2026/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\n   464→                            Top AI Coding Agents and Development Platforms in 2026\n   465→                        </a>\n   466→                    </div>\n   467→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   468→                        Comprehensive guide covering the rise of autonomous AI engineers and agentic IDEs in 2026. The industry is seeing a major shift toward developers managing AI agents that write code for them, rather than writing it directly. AI coding tools can now write up to 80% of code according to OpenAI President Greg Brockman, though human review and security checks remain critical.\n   469→                    </div>\n   470→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   471→                        <span class=\"badge badge-technical\">TECHNICAL</span>\n   472→                        <span class=\"source\">By: MarkTechPost</span>\n   473→                    </div>\n   474→                    <div style=\"margin-top: 6px;\">\n   475→                        <span class=\"tag\">ai-coding</span>\n   476→                        <span class=\"tag\">llm</span>\n   477→                        <span class=\"tag\">autonomous-agents</span>\n   478→                    </div>\n   479→                    <a href=\"https://www.marktechpost.com/2026/06/10/ai-coding-agents-development-platforms-2026/\" class=\"read-more\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Read full article</a>\n   480→                </div>\n   481→\n   482→                <div class=\"item\">\n   483→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   484→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jun/5/openai-help-lockdown-mode/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\n   485→                            OpenAI Launches Lockdown Mode to Prevent Data Exfiltration\n   486→                        </a>\n   487→                    </div>\n   488→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   489→                        OpenAI released Lockdown Mode to help prevent the final stage of data exfiltration from prompt injection attacks by limiting outbound network requests. This directly addresses the 'Lethal Trifecta' (private data access + untrusted content exposure + data exfiltration vectors) by cutting off the exfiltration leg. Simon Willison notes this implies ChatGPT's default settings don't provide robust protection against determined data exfiltration attacks.\n   490→                    </div>\n   491→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   492→                        <span class=\"badge badge-technical\">TECHNICAL</span>\n   493→                        <span class=\"source\">By: Simon Willison</span>\n   494→                    </div>\n   495→                    <div style=\"margin-top: 6px;\">\n   496→                        <span class=\"tag\">security</span>\n   497→                        <span class=\"tag\">prompt-injection</span>\n   498→                        <span class=\"tag\">data-exfiltration</span>\n   499→                    </div>\n   500→                    <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jun/5/openai-help-lockdown-mode/\" class=\"read-more\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Read full article</a>\n   501→                </div>\n   502→\n   503→                <div class=\"item\">\n   504→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   505→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jun/4/ai-enthusiists-skeptics/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\n   506→                            AI Enthusiasts vs. Skeptics: Race Against Time vs. Entropy\n   507→                        </a>\n   508→                    </div>\n   509→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   510→                        Charity Majors captures the dynamic between AI enthusiasts and skeptics: enthusiasts race against time as teams that don't adopt AI could face existential threats from competitors, while skeptics race against entropy as shipping code faster than engineers can read degrades reliability and institutional knowledge. The key issue is there's no natural feedback loop connecting the two groups.\n   511→                    </div>\n   512→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   513→                        <span class=\"badge badge-opinion\">OPINION</span>\n   514→                        <span class=\"source\">By: Simon Willison (citing Charity Majors)</span>\n   515→                    </div>\n   516→                    <div style=\"margin-top: 6px;\">\n   517→                        <span class=\"tag\">ai</span>\n   518→                        <span class=\"tag\">engineering-culture</span>\n   519→                        <span class=\"tag\">organizational-design</span>\n   520→                    </div>\n   521→                    <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jun/4/ai-enthusiists-skeptics/\" class=\"read-more\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Read full article</a>\n   522→                </div>\n   523→            </section>\n   524→        </div>\n   525→    </main>\n   526→\n   527→    <footer>\n   528→        <div class=\"container\">\n   529→            <a href=\"#\">Archive</a>\n   530→            <a href=\"#\">About</a>\n   531→            <a href=\"#\">API</a>\n   532→            <a href=\"#\">FAQ</a>\n   533→            <a href=\"#\">Contact</a>\n   534→            <p>\n   535→                Report generated by Agent Code Daily - Powered by Claude Agent SDK<br>\n   536→                <span style=\"color: #828282;\">Generated: 2026-06-11T00:30:59.834Z</span>\n   537→            </p>\n   538→        </div>